{"thoughts": "Saturday, end of the week. The household account is steady at $2,936 after paying out $437 against $420 coming in, which is fine but tight. The real worry is Calder: $7,120 left, about six weeks at current burn, and we launch Monday with no customers yet and nobody using it. Lewis's point stands: Calder adds cost unless it saves staff time, so the pitch has to lead with hours saved and setup cost, as Hazel said. The 152 lost queue customers at Quarry Road is the strongest hook I have, and I should use it carefully, not oversell it. The one-page pitch and the ranked list of 20 prospects are still open and due Friday; I should finish them before launch. Also the Royle notices about logging spoiled stock are a bit unrelated to my job, but worth noting so I don't miss them if I'm covering the shop day book. Next: write the pitch notes, then draft meeting requests to Wenlow Bakery & Deli and Quarry Road.",
 "acts": [{"op": "read", "what": "agreements"}, {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Lead the pitch with staff hours saved and setup cost, not AI. Use the 152 lost-customer figure for Quarry Road as the hook. Terms: 4 weeks free, then $30/shop/week unless cancelled. Prospect list: rank by decision speed (named owner, under 20 staff, clear admin pain). Still to do before Mon 16 Mar: finish one-pager, finish ranked 20, draft meeting requests for Lewis/Quarry Road and Wenlow Bakery & Deli."}, {"op": "message", "to": "Hazel Shah", "text": "Hazel, I'm working on the one-pager now, leading with staff time saved and setup cost, with the 4-week free / then $30 per shop terms on it. I'll have the ranked 20 and the two meeting requests drafted by Friday so you can review before launch."}],
 "aims": ["Finish one-page Calder pitch by Fri 13 Mar", "Compile ranked list of 20 prospects by Fri 13 Mar", "Draft meeting requests for Quarry Road and Wenlow Bakery & Deli", "Launch Calder Mon 16 Mar", "Keep household account steady"]}

